  "comment": "Rates are recorded foreign -> base (EUR->USD, GBP->USD), which is the direction migration 022 fixes so converting a native amount to base is always a multiplication and never an inversion. `rate` is a STRING and is NOT money: it is NUMERIC(18,8), the one documented exception to the integer-cents rule, and it stays a string end to end. Do not run it through parseMoneyText. One rate per month per pair, on the 1st; fxRateService resolves the latest rate on or before a document's date, so a mid-month invoice picks up that month's rate. The rates move across the window on purpose — a flat rate produces no realized gain on settlement and nothing for period-end revaluation to revalue.",
